//! `app-core`: the platform library every service is built on.
//!
//! - [`config`]: the root `.env` read into a typed [`Config`] (the only place that reads env vars)
//! - [`registry`]: `services.json`, the list of services, their ports and edge routes
//! - [`db`]: the shared SQLite database (WAL) and the migrations in `/migrations`
//! - [`error`]: [`ApiError`], the one JSON error shape of every `/api` endpoint
//! - [`auth`]: the [`AuthUser`] / [`AdminUser`] extractors (session cookie and personal API keys)
//! - [`crypto`]: AES-256-GCM for secrets at rest, random tokens and token hashes
//! - [`settings`]: typed access to the `settings` table
//! - [`caller`]: [`Caller`], the user a request acts for (scopes per-user data)
//! - [`service`]: [`Ctx`], [`service::main`] (one service in its own process) and
//!   [`service::host`] (all of them in `app-all`), the bootstrap shared by all services
//! - [`bridge`]: how services call each other ([`Ctx::call`]): in-process or over HTTP
//! - [`outbound`]: the SSRF-safe client (`ctx.outbound`) for URLs from users, models or webhooks
//! - [`client_ip`]: the client address the edge passes to the services (limits, logs)
//!
//! Services never read env vars, open the database or set up tracing themselves: they are
//! libraries with `build(ctx)` and get a ready [`Ctx`] from [`service::main`] or [`service::host`].

